# MCP Upstream Update

## Purpose

- Use this workflow when updating `UnrealMCP5_6_1` from `chongdashu/unreal-mcp` while preserving Cubeless MCP extensions and UE 5.6.1 compatibility.
- The Cubeless integration branch is `main`.
- The current UE 5.6.1 compatibility branch convention is `codex/ue-5.6.1-compat`.
- The original upstream remote should be named `upstream` and point to `https://github.com/chongdashu/unreal-mcp.git`.
- The Cubeless fork remote should be named `origin` and point to `https://github.com/cubeless2-lgtm/UnrealMCP5_6_1.git`.

## Default Strategy

- Do not rebase or force-push the public default branch `main` by default.
- Start a no-commit merge from `upstream/main`, run verification, then create the merge commit only after verification passes.
- Push only when the user explicitly asks for push intent.
- If the target GitHub repository is still empty, do not assume `origin/main` exists; use an explicit first push for the current branch.
- Keep legacy branches such as `local/pcg-tools` intact unless the user explicitly asks to update, delete, or repoint them.

## Preflight

- Confirm `git status --short --branch` is clean or that all dirty files are intentionally part of the current task.
- Confirm `origin` points to `https://github.com/cubeless2-lgtm/UnrealMCP5_6_1.git`.
- Confirm `upstream` exists and has push disabled or otherwise cannot be pushed to accidentally.
- Fetch `origin` and `upstream` before comparing branches.
- Confirm the active target engine remains `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6`.

## Update Procedure

1. Check out the intended integration branch.
2. If `origin/main` exists, fast-forward local `main` from it before merging upstream.
3. Fetch `upstream`.
4. Start a no-commit merge from `upstream/main`:
   ```powershell
   git merge --no-commit --no-ff upstream/main
   ```
5. Resolve conflicts by preserving:
   - generic `execute_python` bridge support
   - PCG and Blueprint authoring tools
   - AI texture tool safety and cost controls
   - editor map transition safety tools
   - Cubeless analysis and verification scripts
   - embedded `codex/` operating docs
   - UE 5.6.1 compatibility guards and fallbacks
6. Expect modify/delete conflicts on `UnrealMCPBlueprintNodeCommands.cpp` and `UnrealMCPNiagaraCommands.cpp`: this fork split both monoliths on 2026-07-03 into `UnrealMCP*CommandsShared.h` + `UnrealMCP*Commands_Part*.cpp` (same classes, functions moved verbatim; see `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/tooling/unreal-mcp-stability-hardening-2026-07.md` → "Monolith split"). Resolve by keeping the deletion, then hand-port any upstream change into the part file that now holds that handler (search the function name across `Commands/UnrealMCP*Commands_Part*.cpp`; helper changes go into the matching `*Shared.h`).
7. Run Python verification before committing the merge.
8. Commit the pending merge only after verification passes.
9. Run targeted bridge/editor verification when the change touches C++ bridge code, editor sockets, map transition tools, asset writes, or PCG generation.
10. Push only when requested.

## Verification

- Use `Python/scripts/analysis/run_verification.py` as the Python gate source of truth.
- While resolving and correcting conflicts, run the applicable focused profiles from `codex/projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`; use `core` for ordinary Python or AI texture/import source changes and add the affected component profile when needed.
- Do not run `full` after every conflict edit. After the merge result is frozen and before creating the merge commit, run the final checkpoint:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_verification.py --profile full
```

- Focused profiles do not replace `full` at the final upstream checkpoint. Automatic changed-file or path-based skipping is not enabled.

For C++ plugin changes, build against UE 5.6:

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```

## Reporting

- Report upstream commit before/after, merge result, verification result, whether a merge commit was created, and whether a push happened.
- If conflicts, verification failures, or build blockers remain, report the exact files and leave Git state visible. A failed no-commit merge may be resolved and committed, or abandoned with `git merge --abort`.
- Keep reporting scoped to the `UnrealMCP5_6_1` repository unless the user explicitly names an external repository.
